      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1952030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-23T21:51:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In BpfRingbuf, `Init` is protected. The only way to create an instance is with the constructor (which aborts) or `Create` (which returns `unique_ptr`). The nice part is that you won\u0027t ever have an uninitialized or failed-initialized instance. However, I suppose that does diverge from what BpfMap does...\n\nSo with the code today, using `unique_ptr` allows using `Create` and defer initialization until OnStart. Had this use the abort constructor instead, it would be harder to test and need to be initialized upon registration, shortly after boot.\n\nMaking `Init` public would allow deferring initialization as well, but I typically use this pattern based on the advice in https://abseil.io/tips/42. If you want it consistent with BpfMap, I can go add that.",
      "parentUuid": "cf56a653_70999042",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 18
      },
